{"sections": [
  {"key": "arc", "title": "The arc", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Revenue compounded at 14.7% a year from $96.6 billion in FY2017 to $331.8 billion in FY2026 [F1][F10][F221]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The path was a steady climb rather than a step change, with the only slow year FY2023 at 6.9% growth [D311]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "FY2023's slowdown came as Intelligent Cloud and Productivity and Business Processes grew while More Personal Computing declined on Windows and Devices [P39][D932]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "FY2026 reaccelerated to 17.8% growth, driven by Microsoft Cloud, with Intelligent Cloud led by Azure and Productivity and Business Processes by Microsoft 365 Commercial cloud [D472][P17]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "drivers", "title": "What drove growth", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Microsoft Cloud reached 64.6% of revenue in FY2026 and contributed 16.2pp of the year's growth [D566][D568]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Server products and cloud services revenue rose 31% on Azure and other cloud services, which grew 41% on demand across workloads [P12][D641]."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Microsoft 365 Commercial products and cloud services added 5.1pp of growth, with cloud revenue up 17% on Copilot and E5 [D649][P14]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating income grew 20.8% against revenue growth of 17.8%, an incremental margin of 53.3% [D473][D472][D498]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Diluted EPS grew 31.6% against net income growth of 31.3%, with the diluted share count down 0.2% [D476][D474][D493]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "margins", "title": "Margins and costs", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating margin reached 46.8% in FY2026, a window high against a 41.7% median and 30.1% low [F50][D974][D975][D973]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Gross margin slipped 0.9pp to 67.9%, below its 68.2% median, as cost of revenue rose 21.1% against 17.8% revenue growth [F30][D486][D981][D489][D472]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Intelligent Cloud gross margin percentage fell on continued AI infrastructure investment and mix shift to Azure, partly offset by Azure efficiency gains [P11]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "R&D fell to 10.7% of revenue, a window low, and selling and marketing to 8.0%, lifting operating margin 1.2pp [D450][D985][D451][D487]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Net margin rose 4.2pp to 40.3%, helped by $6.5 billion of net OpenAI investment gains in other income [D488][F70][P7]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "cash", "title": "Cash conversion", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Operating cash flow reached $182.9 billion in FY2026, 55.1% of revenue [F100][D457]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "That increase was primarily due to higher cash received from customers and lower cash paid for income taxes [P1]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Free cash flow fell 6.5% to $67.0 billion, a 20.2% margin and window low, as capex rose 79.6% to $115.9 billion [F120][D478][D456][D982][F110][D479]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Free cash flow was 0.50x net income against a 0.91x median, and capex ran 3.38x D&A [D460][D990][D461]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "balance_sheet", "title": "Balance sheet and capital allocation", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Net cash was $72.9 billion, 22.0% of revenue, in the 83rd percentile of six software peers against a -7.2% median [D465][D466][D1006][D1007]."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Total debt fell 6.6% to $40.3 billion while cash and investments rose 2.9% to $113.2 billion [D464][D495][D463][D494]."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Buybacks and dividends of $48.7 billion were 72.7% of free cash flow [D467][D468]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Return on average equity was 34.0%, below the 38.8% peer median, as equity grew 28.8% [D471][D1011][D482]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "red_flags", "title": "Red flags", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Free cash flow has run below 80% of net income for two years, at 0.70x in FY2025 and 0.50x in FY2026, the window low [R1][D406][D460][D988]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The gap reflects the capex build, with additions to property and equipment up $51.4 billion in FY2026 [P1][D479]."},
    {"type": "judgement", "text": "This is a deliberate AI infrastructure bet rather than an earnings-quality problem, but it leaves free cash flow margin at 20.2% against a 34.7% peer median [D456][D1003]."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "The FY2017 liquidity break means cash and investments and net cash omit short-term investments that year, so cross-gap comparisons are unreliable [R6][X158]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "watch", "title": "What to watch", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Free cash flow margin: a recovery above the 30.3% window median would confirm capex is peaking, while a print below the 20.2% FY2026 low would extend the squeeze [D984][D982]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating margin: holding above the 41.7% median would confirm the cost discipline, while a drop below it would reverse the FY2026 high of 46.8% [D975][D974]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Intelligent Cloud margin: a move back above the 42.0% FY2025 level would signal AI infrastructure costs are absorbing, while a further fall from 41.3% would extend the decline [D962][D963]."}
  ]}
